1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,641
This is Crypto Bot, running live.

2
00:00:02,691 --> 00:00:05,097
Once a day it decides whether to hold

3
00:00:05,147 --> 00:00:08,351
Bitcoin, Ethereum and Solana, or wait in dollars.

4
00:00:08,401 --> 00:00:11,537
I'll start it on Solana in simulation mode: real

5
00:00:11,587 --> 00:00:14,791
Jupiter quotes and routes, virtual USDC, no risk.

6
00:00:14,841 --> 00:00:18,575
The own wallet option runs the same flow with real swaps.

7
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:23,359
Within seconds it makes its first decision.

8
00:00:23,409 --> 00:00:27,191
Each coin is above three of its four moving averages, so the bot

9
00:00:27,241 --> 00:00:31,144
holds a quarter of the capital in each and keeps the rest in USDC.

10
00:00:31,194 --> 00:00:33,839
The feed explains every trade in plain words,

11
00:00:33,889 --> 00:00:36,833
and the next decision comes after the daily close.

12
00:00:37,633 --> 00:00:39,779
Advanced mode shows the reasoning.

13
00:00:39,829 --> 00:00:43,138
For every coin: the daily close, its distance to the

14
00:00:43,188 --> 00:00:46,691
20, 50, 100 and 200-day averages, and the target share.

15
00:00:46,741 --> 00:00:51,212
Today each coin is below its 20-day average and above the other three.

16
00:00:51,262 --> 00:00:54,183
Below are the venue and on-chain settings, the

17
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:58,058
decision journal, and a live log of everything the bot does.

18
00:01:00,358 --> 00:01:03,419
For more history, here is the same app replaying

19
00:01:03,469 --> 00:01:06,466
the strategy on real 2026 prices since January.

20
00:01:06,516 --> 00:01:09,253
It is up about eleven percent, while simply

21
00:01:09,303 --> 00:01:12,040
holding the three coins lost about fifteen.

22
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:16,058
And the interface switches to Russian and Armenian on the fly.

23
00:01:16,858 --> 00:01:20,706
The equity curve marks every trade, and the drawdown panel shows how

24
00:01:20,756 --> 00:01:24,546
far the capital fell from its peak: under twenty percent this year.

25
00:01:24,596 --> 00:01:28,272
When the trends came back in late summer, the bot bought back in.

26
00:01:28,322 --> 00:01:30,908
The journal filters trades, checks and errors.

27
00:01:33,208 --> 00:01:34,689
Back to the live session.

28
00:01:34,739 --> 00:01:39,281
Stopping is one button: the bot sells everything back to USDC and shows the

29
00:01:39,331 --> 00:01:44,608
result, about a dollar below the start, mostly the round-trip cost of Jupiter's quotes.

30
00:01:44,658 --> 00:01:48,833
Crypto Bot: one slow decision a day, from your own wallet, on Solana.
